WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.936
 Bladesmiths, congratulations.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.537
You fellas have made
it into the final round

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:05.571
of this competition.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.073
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:12.812
to recreate this iconic
weapon from history,

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.981
General George
Washington's lion-headed

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:17.216
cuttoe Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:18.551
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.526
TYLER: So my billet's going to
be made out of 1084 and 15N20.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.829
Really good contrasting
steels for Damascus.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:33.799
The last time I did my sabre
build for the army episode,

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:35.368
I went with the Damascus.

00:00:35.401 --> 00:00:38.138
The Damascus, it is a
risk because there's

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.973
multiple things that could
go wrong, from cold shots

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.575
to stress fractures.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:46.278
But as long as my blade does
perform as I expect it to,

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:47.813
my Damascus is going
to be that thing

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.115
that puts me over the top.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:54.921 line:0%
GENE: Here we are again back
in Springfield, Virginia,

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:56.322 line:7%
at my home forge.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:01:01.327
The plan for today is to cut
out a billet for the sword.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.129
Well, this wood anvil, as they
call it, or the log [inaudible]

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:08.234
method to put a gentle
arc in the blade.

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.737
That's the same log that I
used for the Mameluke sword

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.039
for the Marine competition.

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:14.140
It worked before.

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:15.675
If it's not broken,
don't fix it.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.013 line:7%
TYLER: Day two.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:21.147
I got to get this
blade quenched today,

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.915
and I'm going to
make some changes

00:01:22.981 --> 00:01:24.818
to the way I do it in my forge.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:28.121
I'm going to try
using the tube method.

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.156
The main goal is
to take this tube

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:33.793
and just turn it into
a nice long, hot oven.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.263
Had a little bit of issues
getting even heat last time.

00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:39.899
So I think with that tube
it should give me a nice,

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:42.869
more even, controlled heat.

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:46.638
I don't hear any cracks,
pings, or anything like that.

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:47.540
I nailed it.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.109
It's exactly what
I need it to be.

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:55.014
[banjo]

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.215
 Anyway.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:58.151
Day four finally here.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.519
I'm feeling ready.

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:01.720
I have a plan, and I have
some hurdles to get over.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:04.791
The biggest one [inaudible]
is that lion-head pommel.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.192
First thing this
morning, I'm going

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.062
to put that thing in plaster
of Paris and let it set.

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.063
Wonder if I should
do it with pewter?

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:14.333
You don't have to get
pewter nearly as hot.

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:16.469
It will be shiny and
look just like silver.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.474
It looks like garbage.

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:24.644
I think I'm going to go with
the silver one just because

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.647
of the look of the silver.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:29.682
Right now I need to
finish the lion head,

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.719
polish everything,
and sharpen the blade,

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.388
try to take some weight off
anywhere that I possibly can,

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.690
and then put it all together.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.557
Woo!

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:39.392
Done.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.927 line:7%
It's done.

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.363 line:7%
 Dave four, final day.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.599
I've never carved
a pommel before,

00:02:46.665 --> 00:02:48.667
so I don't know how
long it's going to take,

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.203
and I'm going to have to
put some time into it.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.906
So I'm just profiling
from one way right now

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:57.744
the shape of the lion's head
to kind of refine it to what

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.612
my final shape is going to be.

00:02:59.678 --> 00:03:02.781
And then I start removing some
more material, a little fine

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:04.516
tuning with my rotary tool.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:08.787
It pretty much looks
like a lion to me.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:13.293
 All right, veterans,
welcome to the kill test.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:16.128
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:03:16.161 --> 00:03:17.830
I will take your weapon
and deliver killing

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.898
blows to this pig carcass.

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:20.766
Tyler, you're up first.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.535
Ready?

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.236
[laughter]

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:26.639
 I'm ready.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:30.610
[music playing]

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:51.397
 All right, Tyler, your handle
construction, just right.

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:54.533
Your edge is very sharp.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.237
Overall, sir, this
sabre will kill.

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:00.172
 Perfect.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:01.307
 All right, Gene,
your turn, sir.

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.207
Are you ready?

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.910
 Let's do this, Doug.

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:08.481
[music playing]

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.805
 All right, Gene,
this is a heavy sword

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:34.040
and very forward heavy.

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:36.509
But when you have a forward
heavy blade that you're hitting

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:40.613
that meets resistance,
a cylindrical, almost

00:04:40.646 --> 00:04:44.350
circular handle makes
it twist in my hand.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:47.853
So probably there's a reason
why the chain came off.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.056
But your blade is sharp.

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:50.823
It will kill.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:59.998
 All right, gentlemen, December
25, 1776, George Washington

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:03.402
leads the Continental Army
across a frozen Delaware River

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:06.005
to attack the Hessians
at Trenton, New Jersey.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.773
And he probably didn't chip
his way through the ice,

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.842
but that's not going to
keep us from our strength

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:13.246
test, the ice-block chop.

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.247
Tyler, you're up first.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:15.114
Are you ready?
- Oh, yeah.

00:05:15.147 --> 00:05:15.848
Yeah.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:16.916
Let's do it.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:29.796
[music playing]

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:49.549
 All right, so Tyler,
your chain fell off,

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:52.251
but there's no
damage on your edge.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.453
Your handle's comfortable.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.020
Other than the
chain, you nailed it.

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:55.788
 Thanks.

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:56.789
 Good job.

00:05:56.856 --> 00:05:58.056
All right, Gene.

00:05:58.123 --> 00:05:59.058
 Do it.

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:01.026
[laughter]

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:05.031
[music playing]

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:28.487
 All right, Gene,
your blade's edge

00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:30.456
is still there and still sharp.

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:33.926
The issue is the rest
of your chain fell off,

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.461
and it's picked up a bend.

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:38.597
I have less issue with
that and more issue

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:40.232
with this polished handle.

00:06:40.298 --> 00:06:42.234
It's just hard to hold on to.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:47.206
But it is strong, and it does
have an edge, so good job.

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:49.808
 Oorah.

00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:52.377
 All right, veterans,
our sharpness test today

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:54.914
is the Hessian charge.

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:58.584
This is all about what your
edge will do to these dummies.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.819
Tyler, you're up first.

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:00.686
You ready for this?

00:07:00.719 --> 00:07:01.421
 Yep.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.898
[music playing]

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:31.917
 All right, Tyler, the
weight of your weapon

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:33.853
does prevent me from
going very fast,

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:36.522
but you have a very sharp
edge all the way through.

00:07:36.588 --> 00:07:38.490
Your weapon, sir, it will cut.

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:39.825
 Thank you.

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:41.260
 All right, Gene,
it's your turn, sir.

00:07:41.326 --> 00:07:42.862
Are you ready?
- Let's do this, Doug.

00:07:51.203 --> 00:07:54.740
[music playing]

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:16.162
 All right, Gene, to be able
to maintain a good grip on this,

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:17.696
more of the cuts
I create are more

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.832
impact as opposed
to a slash where

00:08:19.865 --> 00:08:21.433
it cuts all the way through.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.935
So you have some
cuts here that are

00:08:23.001 --> 00:08:27.106
more nicks, deep nicks, because
you have a very sharp edge.

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:31.076
And for this test, sir,
your weapon will cut.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:33.579
 Awesome.

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:35.414
 Tyler, Gene, first
of all, I want to thank

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.216
you both for your service.

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:38.718
You're both
champions in my mind.

00:08:38.751 --> 00:08:41.820
You've already won
your branch divisions,

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:44.957
but there can only be one
Battle of the Branches champion,

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:49.594
and you'll walk out of here
with a check for $50,000.

00:08:49.661 --> 00:08:55.067
And that champion is Tyler.

00:08:55.101 --> 00:08:55.868
Congratulations.

00:08:55.935 --> 00:08:58.103
You are the Battle
of the Branches

00:08:58.170 --> 00:08:59.738
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:04.343
Gene, please
surrender your blade.

00:09:04.409 --> 00:09:05.745
 There's a lot of
Marines out there,

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.846
and there's a lot of great
guys in the Marine Corps.

00:09:07.913 --> 00:09:09.514
And so for me to stand
here and represent

00:09:09.581 --> 00:09:11.583
them is pretty humbling.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.652
I learned too that
it's not about just

00:09:13.718 --> 00:09:15.488
the metal being forged in fire.

00:09:15.521 --> 00:09:17.089
I feel like I've
been forged in fire.

00:09:17.156 --> 00:09:20.293
And it's how you handle the ups
and downs, the wins and losses,

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:22.528
and it will determine real
quick how you've been heat

00:09:22.594 --> 00:09:23.829
treated throughout your life.

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:27.766
 Tyler, congratulations.

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:31.337
You overcame every obstacle
set in front of you.

00:09:31.404 --> 00:09:33.105
You beat out all
the other smiths,

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:35.074
and now you're the
Battle of the Branches

00:09:35.141 --> 00:09:36.375
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:41.647
That's a title that comes with
a check for $50,000 and, most

00:09:41.713 --> 00:09:44.250
importantly, bragging rights.

00:09:44.283 --> 00:09:45.450
Good job, my brother.

00:09:45.517 --> 00:09:49.254
Please present your
blade to the judges.

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:50.756
 I'm super excited.

00:09:50.823 --> 00:09:52.892
When this whole thing
started, I had no idea how

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:54.159
it was all going to turn out.

00:09:54.193 --> 00:09:56.862
It feels good to have
represented the Army.

00:09:56.928 --> 00:10:03.035
The fact that I just won
$50,000 is starting to set in.

00:10:03.068 --> 00:10:06.371
I'm Sergeant Tyler Hackbarth,
and I'm the new Battle

00:10:06.438 --> 00:10:08.808
of the Branches champion.

